.TH PANOD 1 "2026-09-19" "panora" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
panod \- Panora clipboard history daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B panod
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B panod
watches the CLIPBOARD selection (and, when enabled, PRIMARY) of the running
desktop session, passes every change through the privacy engine and stores
the allowed content encrypted on disk. Clients such as
.BR panora-gui (1)
and
.BR panora-cli (1)
talk to it over a private Unix socket.
.PP
The daemon runs in the foreground. The Debian package installs it as the
.B panod.service
systemd user unit, which starts with the graphical session; enable it with
.IP
.nf
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now panod.service
.fi
.SH BACKENDS
The backend is chosen from the session:
.TP
.B x11
XFIXES change events, native selection ownership on recall (INCR for large
payloads), XTEST for instant paste.
.TP
.B wayland
.I ext\-data\-control\-v1
or
.I zwlr\-data\-control\-v1
(GNOME 48+, KDE Plasma, Sway, Hyprland, \&...). The protocols expose no client
identity, so the application exclusion list cannot fire here; the password
manager MIME gate still applies.
.TP
.B gnome\-bridge
GNOME 47 and older on Wayland: clipboard changes arrive from the Panora GNOME
Shell extension over the session bus, which must be enabled.
.SH PRIVACY
Content flagged by a password manager
.RI ( x\-kde\-passwordManagerHint ,
.IR org.nspasteboard.ConcealedType ,
\&...) is never read. Applications on the exclusion list, and everything while
private mode is on, are skipped before any payload is transferred.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/panora/config.toml
Configuration; re-read on
.B panora-cli reload
and when the settings dialog saves.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/panora/history.db
Entry metadata and encrypted previews (SQLite, mode 0600).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/panora/blobs/
Encrypted, content-addressed payloads.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/panora.sock
IPC socket (mode 0600, peer UID checked).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, for example
.BR info " (default) or " debug .
Output goes to the journal when started by systemd.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR panora-cli (1),
.BR panora-gui (1),
.BR panora-doctor (1)
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/ygkali/panora/issues
